  "original_script": "Stop building simple wrapper apps. The way we build AI is changing completely. In just two years, we went from simple chat prompts to smart systems that can work together.\n\nAt first, we just wrote simple prompts. Then, we used RAG to give the model real files and documents to read. After that, we made single agents that could use tools. Today, we are in the era of Agentic AI—where a team of specialized agents work together to solve big, complex goals.\n\nAnd companies are adopting this very fast. Studies show that ninety-six percent of large I-T companies are starting to use agents. In fact, AI agent startups have already raised over two billion dollars, and the market is expected to reach nearly two hundred billion dollars by twenty thirty-four.\n\nWe are moving from a single model to a team of agents. But working in a team has its own challenges.\n\nGood question, Riya. For simple tasks, a team is too much. But for complex workflows, a single prompt gets confused and makes mistakes. Having multiple specialized agents lets us divide the work. This makes it much easier to test, fix, and scale the system.\n\nSo how complex can these agents actually get? In our next video, we will look at the four levels of AI agents."
